#: ../../../install.rst:90
msgid "Independent install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:92
msgid ""
"When xonsh is used as a core shell, it is necessary to keep the Python "
"environment with xonsh stable, predictable, and independent of system "
"changes. Lightweight environment managers such as ``venv``, ``pipx``, or "
"``rye`` do not fully address this requirement. Package managers that can "
"install fully isolated Python environments as a core feature, such as "
"Miniconda or Micromamba, should be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:99
msgid "Linux / macOS / WSL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:101
msgid "Install Xonsh independently using Micromamba:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:103
msgid ""
"$ TARGET_DIR=$HOME/.local/xonsh-env PYTHON_VER=3.11 XONSH_VER='xonsh[full]' "
"\\\n"
"  /bin/bash -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://xon.sh/install/mamba-install-xonsh."
"sh)\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:108
msgid "Learn more: `Mamba installer <install_mamba.html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:112
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:116
msgid ""
"The installation instructions for Windows were recently updated. If you run "
"into any issues, please report them to the `issue tracker <https://github."
"com/xonsh/xonsh/issues>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:120
msgid ""
"We provide an experimental Xonsh installer for Windows (no admin rights "
"required). Download the ``.exe`` from the `Xonsh WinGet releases page "
"<https://github.com/xonsh/xonsh-winget/releases>`_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:123
msgid "``inno6`` — for Windows 10/11 (latest Python 3)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:124
msgid "``inno5`` — for Windows 8.1+ (pinned to Python 3.13)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:126
msgid "Or install via the script (no admin rights required):"
