#: ../../../install.rst:134
msgid "Package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:136
msgid "**pip:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:138
msgid ""
"You can install the xonsh package from PyPI with any pip-compatible "
"installer (``pip``, ``pipx``, ``uv``, ``rye``, ``poetry``, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:141
msgid "$ pip install 'xonsh[full]'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:145
msgid ""
"Pip can also install the most recent xonsh source code from the `xonsh "
"project repository <https://github.com/xonsh/xonsh>`_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:148
msgid ""
"$ pip install 'https://github.com/xonsh/xonsh/archive/main."
"zip#egg=xonsh[full]'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:152
msgid "**mamba:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:154
msgid "$ mamba install xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:158
msgid "**conda:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:160
msgid ""
"$ conda config --add channels conda-forge\n"
"$ conda install xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:167
msgid "AppImage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:169
msgid ""
"Xonsh is available as a single AppImage bundled with Python, allowing you to "
"run it on Linux without installation:"
