#: ../../../install.rst:265
msgid "Updating xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:267
msgid "How you update xonsh depends on the install method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:269
msgid "**xonsh installed via pip**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:271
msgid ""
"If xonsh was installed via pip (possibly into a virtual environment), you "
"can update it from within xonsh itself using :ref:`xpip <aliases-xpip>` — a "
"predefined alias pointing to the ``pip`` command associated with the Python "
"executable that runs the current xonsh session:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:276
msgid ""
"@ xpip install --upgrade xonsh  # install the latest release\n"
"@ xpip install -U --force-reinstall git+https://github.com/xonsh/xonsh  # "
"install from the repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:281
msgid ""
"**On Windows** the running ``xonsh.exe`` is locked by the OS, so pip cannot "
"replace it from inside xonsh itself. Grab the interpreter path with :ref:"
"`xcontext <aliases-xcontext>`, leave the shell, then run pip from another "
"terminal (``cmd``, PowerShell, etc.):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:286
msgid ""
"@ xcontext            # note the \"xpython\" path\n"
"@ exit                # release the lock on xonsh.exe\n"
"> <xpython> -m pip install --upgrade xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:292
msgid "**xonsh installed via a package manager**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:294
msgid ""
"If you installed xonsh via a package manager, it is recommended to update it "
"through the package manager's appropriate command. For example, on macOS "
"with homebrew:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:298
msgid "$ brew upgrade xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:306
msgid "Setting xonsh as the default shell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:308
msgid ""
"Setting xonsh as your default login shell is **not recommended**. Xonsh is a "
"full-featured shell and can technically be used as a login shell, but since "
"it is not POSIX-compatible, system scripts and tooling that expect a POSIX "
"shell may misbehave. Use it only if you clearly understand the purpose and "
"consequences — see the rationale in `Before Installing`_ above. The "
"recommended practice is to create a xonsh profile in your terminal emulator "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:316
msgid ""
"If you still want to use xonsh as your default shell, you will have to add "
"xonsh to ``/etc/shells`` and switch:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:319
msgid ""
"$ which xonsh\n"
"# which xonsh >> /etc/shells\n"
"$ chsh -s $(which xonsh)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:325
msgid ""
"You will have to log out and log back in before the changes take effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:329
msgid "GitHub Actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:331
msgid ""
"The `xonsh/actions <https://github.com/xonsh/actions>`_ repository provides "
"a composite action that installs xonsh on a GitHub Actions runner, so "
"subsequent steps can run xonsh code natively. Tested on ``ubuntu-latest``, "
"``macos-latest``, and ``windows-latest``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:335
msgid ""
"Declare ``defaults.run.shell: xonsh {0}`` once for the whole job and every "
"``run:`` block in that job executes as xonsh:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:338
msgid ""
"jobs:\n"
"  my-job:\n"
"    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n"
"    defaults:\n"
"      run:\n"
"        shell: xonsh {0}\n"
"    steps:\n"
"      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n"
"      - uses: xonsh/actions@v1\n"
"\n"
"      - run: |\n"
"          echo \"hello from xonsh\"\n"
"          $PATH.append('/mypath')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:354
msgid ""
"Or set ``shell: xonsh {0}`` on individual steps when only some should run as "
"xonsh:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:356
msgid ""
"jobs:\n"
"  my-job:\n"
"    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n"
"    steps:\n"
"      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n"
"      - uses: xonsh/actions@v1\n"
"\n"
"      - name: Run xonsh\n"
"        shell: xonsh {0}\n"
"        run: |\n"
"          echo \"hello from xonsh\"\n"
"          $PATH.append('/mypath')\n"
"          print($PATH)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install.rst:372
msgid ""
"See the `xonsh/actions README <https://github.com/xonsh/actions>`_ for "
"inputs, outputs, and reusable workflows for testing xontribs."
msgstr ""
